  "note": "Size and SHA-256 pins for the companion Rust bundle `gpuwm-global fetch-doors` stages into ~/.gpuwm/global-doors, beside the engine's own bundle rather than inside it.  The bundle carries the doors `arwen_global.doors.doors_from_bundle('gpuwm-global')` names that its release carries (doors.carried_by): six binaries no published gpuwm bridge bundle carries at all (rw_atms, rw_gnssro, rw_ndbc, rw_igra2, rw_amv, rw_wis2) and two the engine's bundle carries under the same filename in an older build that has none of the subcommands this package calls (rw_asos, rw_goes).  From v0.1.3 it also carries the two libraries built from this package's own rust/ workspace and stamped with this package's commit: rw_global_coldstart (the cold start's analysis regrid and ln(p) remap) and global_render_kernels (the render tapes' regrid and column and the regional translation); a bundle pinned for an earlier release does not carry them (doors.Door.since), and a package version at or past a door's since with pins older than it is refused by tests/test_doors_bundle.py.  This file is written by tools/build_door_bundle.py from the exact bytes a release published, never by hand.  `platforms` is empty until the first release is cut, and `gpuwm-global fetch-doors` reports that as 'no companion bundle has been published yet' rather than inventing a download URL.  If the engine takes the observation crates onto its own line, this file shrinks to the two package libraries.",
